{% extends "layouts/page.njk" %}

{% block schema %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "CollectionPage",
        "@id": "{{ site.url }}/trades/#collection",
        "name": "Tradie websites by trade",
        "description": {{ description | dump | safe }},
        "inLanguage": "en-NZ",
        "isPartOf": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#website" },
        "publisher": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" },
        "hasPart": [{% for t in trades %}
          {
            "@type": "WebPage",
            "@id": "{{ site.url }}/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/",
            "name": {{ t.heading | dump | safe }},
            "url": "{{ site.url }}/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/"
          }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>
{% endblock %}

{% block prose %}
<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>{{ site.priceDisplay }} flat, live in {{ site.buildDays }}</strong>, whichever trade you're in. Copywriting, local SEO, .nz domain and Google Business Profile setup included, with the Jobs In {{ site.guaranteeDays }} Guarantee.</p>
</div>

<h2>Pick your trade</h2>
<div class="hub-grid">
  {%- for t in trades %}
  <a class="hub-card" href="/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/">
    <strong>{{ t.trade }}s</strong>
    <span>{{ t.intro | truncate(105) }}</span>
  </a>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>

<h2>Why we build by trade rather than by template</h2>
<p>Most web companies will build for anyone, which sounds like flexibility and works like a tax. Every job starts from scratch, so it takes six weeks and costs four figures before anyone has written a word.</p>
<p>We only build for trades. That means we already know an electrician's emergency traffic behaves nothing like a builder's renovation research, that a plumber publishing their callout fee converts better than one who won't, and that a painter has no licence to point at so the whole page has to work harder. None of that gets rediscovered on your invoice.</p>
<p>It also has a limit worth stating: if you need e-commerce, a booking platform or a custom integration, we're the wrong outfit and we'll say so on the call.</p>

<h2>Not on the list?</h2>
<p>We build for every trade — the nine above are just the ones with pages so far. Concreters, glaziers, plasterers, fencers, scaffolders, arborists, HVAC: same price, same timeline, same guarantee.</p>
<p><a href="/#contact">Tell us your trade</a> and we'll write it around what you actually do.</p>

